  "notes": [
   "A vendored upstream that is a real repository with its own history, mounted as a gitlink and then bumped to a released commit. The companion is built first, into a sibling directory, because a gitlink names a commit and a fixture pointing at one that does not exist is a broken repository rather than a fixture. `git fsck --strict` inside the result is what proves the gitlink was written the way git wants it, including the git dir living inside the parent at `.git/modules/<name>`."
